S10.2D-R3.2 acquisition-state decoupling diagnosis
Date: 2026-09-06
Scope: source-only Control correction

Observed conflict

The R3 controller's mark-ready action used one database update to mark the
runtime observation green, set wms_real_acquisition_ready=true and create
real_acquisition_baseline_start. This coupled a technical acceptance result to
the separate operator/business decision to activate real acquisition.

Active contract inventory

- The active controller owned the conflicting update and its status output.
- The active manifest and SSOT described the same coupled transition.
- The existing Application migration already supports the required intermediate
  state: pre_acquisition_readiness=GREEN,
  wms_real_acquisition_ready=false and real_acquisition_baseline_start=NULL.
- No active health contract, release contract, evidence validator or growth
  report independently inferred acquisition activation from technical
  readiness. Historical evidence was not modified.

Corrected storage mapping

- WMS_REAL_ACQUISITION_TECHNICALLY_READY maps to
  pre_acquisition_readiness=GREEN.
- REAL_ACQUISITION_ACTIVE maps to the legacy storage field
  wms_real_acquisition_ready=true.
- REAL_ACQUISITION_BASELINE_START maps to
  real_acquisition_baseline_start and is created only with a future S10.2E
  acquisition-GO decision.

Minimal correction

The R3 mark-ready update changes only pre_acquisition_readiness to GREEN. It
leaves acquisition inactive and the baseline null, reports
WAITING_OPERATOR_ACQUISITION_GO and disables automatic link seeding. A bounded
state-matrix guard accepts only false/false/null, true/false/null and
true/true/timestamp. Rollback resets only an inactive, null-baseline current R3
state and refuses an active acquisition state.

Risk and rollback

The material risks are an early baseline, accidental traffic activation,
incorrect rollback and contamination of pre-acquisition reporting. The state
guard and regression matrix fail closed for each. The source can be restored
from the verified pre-change Git bundle. No server backup is needed because no
server or runtime mutation is authorized or performed.

Boundaries

The canonical Application SHA, migration 0029, AF_INET correction, runtime
failure taxonomy, publication rotation, moderation, latency, Telegram and all
Adult/AVS/payment/publishing/beta/production gates remain unchanged.
